{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented and pushed for review as Gerrit change 2362 (commit 6598b34be0bc,\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2362).\n\nPlan-review gate: PASS + signed attestation on the 4th review run; claimed without any force\noverride. The three blocking findings the gate caught were all real and all changed the design:\n\n1. G6 — mirroring autodeploy step 5b verbatim would have copied its `record_backoff_failure`\n   (the REVIEW-BOT recorder, which writes $BACKOFF_FILE and gates the whole script). The new gate\n   calls `record_mcp_backoff_failure`; 5b's own defect is filed separately as\n   `prespinal-gem-kinkajou` and pinned by a backoff-file-independence assertion in the new test.\n2. T12 — asked how the gate behaves on an auth-enabled server. It is unaffected: the probe drives\n   the session manager directly, never RequireAuthMiddleware, so an auth-enabled boot reports the\n   same truthful transport result. Pinned by\n   `test_an_auth_enabled_server_still_reports_a_successful_handshake`.\n3. G6 — the strongest one: with the probe Host drawn from the allowlist, a WRONG-but-nonempty\n   allowlist passes by construction, so the check could not catch the failure the ticket's own\n   narrative describes. Probe-host precedence now starts from the deployment's DECLARED public\n   resource URL (`REBAR_MCP_AUTH_RESOURCE_SERVER_URL`), which is declared independently of the\n   allowlist, then falls back to a literal allowlist entry, a materialized `host:*`, and the bind.\n   Pinned by `test_allowlist_that_admits_the_wrong_hostname_fails`.\n\nVerification: 110 tests pass across the five affected modules; `make lint` and `make typecheck`\nexit 0. Mutation check — 10 production edits reverted individually, each targeted test failing by\nreturn code, every seed confirmed applied: probe-host precedence, the 200 status check, the\ntimeout scope, the lifespan ORDERING, the /health field, the `http.disconnect` in `receive` (the\nobserved hang), the lifespan wrap, the `run_http_with_grace` install call, the deploy-gate\npredicate, and the backoff recorder. 10/10 killed. The install-call mutant initially SURVIVED —\nthe wiring line had no test — so\n`test_run_http_with_grace_hands_uvicorn_an_app_that_runs_the_handshake` was added, which drives\nthe exact app handed to uvicorn through the raw ASGI lifespan.\n\nNot closing: waiting on LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on 2362."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787968193603784001,"uuid":"6434a289-33f0-4833-92fd-44afcaad1d54"}